#X text 250 20 Whistle: the chord whistled - a pure tone two octaves up with a slow \, unsteady pitch and a vibrato that grows with brightness \, breath around it (noise in a narrow band on the tone) \, the octave below faintly for body \; one tone \, each side its own breath (two tones a hair apart would beat away in mono);
